---
import WorkLayout from '../../layouts/WorkLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import StriveChat from '../../components/sketches/StriveChat.astro';

const description = "Strive's chat agent renders answers as live, interactive UI. The frontend behind it — a from-scratch streaming engine, a block and slot vocabulary, and the design system it runs on — is work I've helped build from day zero.";
---
<WorkLayout
  title="Strive AI — generative UI chat"
  description={description}
  ogDescription="Strive's chat agent renders answers as live, interactive UI. The frontend behind it: a from-scratch streaming engine, a block and slot vocabulary, and the design system it runs on."
  eyebrow="Strivelabs · Founding engineer · 2024 → now"
  heading="Strive AI"
  facts={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Founding engineer · frontend owner' },
    { label: 'Scope', value: 'Gen-UI engine, end to end' },
    { label: 'Status', value: 'In production, still shipping' },
  ]}
  link={{ href: 'https://strivelabs.ai/', label: 'strivelabs.ai' }}
  schema={{
    name: 'Strive AI — generative UI chat',
    url: 'https://strivelabs.ai/',
    description: 'The chat surface Strive agents reach the user through: a from-scratch streaming engine, a block and slot vocabulary, and rich generative interfaces rendered live.',
    inLanguage: 'en',
    keywords: 'generative UI, AI chat, streaming, React 19, TypeScript, design systems, design engineering',
  }}
>
  <StriveChat slot="sketch" />

  <Fragment slot="lede">Marketing engine that answers in <mark class="hl">live interfaces, not paragraphs</mark>. I've been on the frontend since day zero — building the streaming engine, the block vocabulary, and the gen-UI foundation the platform runs on.</Fragment>

  <h2>The setup</h2>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li>Marketing used to run on pre-built dashboards, spreadsheets, and slide decks — each one kept alive by hand, and collaborating meant chasing whoever "owned" the file.</li>
    <li>The agentic era handed us a better primitive: just <em>ask</em>. So we bet the platform on chat — but chat that answers in rich, generative UI, not walls of text.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The bet we made</h2>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li>Gen UI wasn't really a category yet. None of us were AI experts — we learned it hands-on: benchmark, borrow, break, repeat.</li>
    <li>We test-drove the shortcuts — Vercel AI SDK, Thesys, a few others. Promising, but not quite there yet for what we needed.</li>
    <li>So we chose to build the engine in-house. It's the core of the platform, and owning it outright gave us the flexibility to shape it around marketing — more responsibility, but worth it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What's under the chat</h2>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li><strong>Blocks</strong> — the atom. Charts, tables, forms, controls, whole interactive surfaces the model composes an answer from.</li>
    <li><strong>A canvas beside the thread</strong> — a workspace for things too big to inline. We landed on it early, and tuned it for agentic, marketing-specific work rather than a generic doc pane.</li>
    <li><strong>Contracts</strong> — every streamed block is validated at the boundary, so a confused model degrades gracefully instead of blanking the screen.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where it got interesting</h2>
  <p>The first cut asked the model for one giant JSON payload holding every block. Fine — until answers got complex, and then malformed JSON, truncations, silent retries.</p>
  <!-- .flow is white-space: pre, so the line breaks below are the layout. -->
  <div class="flow" role="img" aria-label="Before: the model returns a single JSON blob that is parsed into progressive blocks. After: the model emits individual tool calls, each parsed on its own, with plain text streaming alongside.">
<b class="bad">BEFORE</b>
LLM ─▶ one JSON blob ─▶ CONTENT_STREAM ─▶ parser ─▶ blocks

<b class="good">AFTER</b>
LLM ─▶ individual tool calls ─▶ TOOL_STREAM_START/CONTENT
    ─▶ per-tool parsing ─▶ blocks
    (plain text keeps streaming alongside)</div>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li>Rebuilt around individual tool calls: each block parses on its own, so one bad block can't sink the whole answer.</li>
    <li>Richer answers just mean <em>more</em> tool calls, not a bigger blob — complexity became additive.</li>
  </ul>

  <blockquote>Chat is the easy part. The harness underneath it is the product.</blockquote>

  <h2>Under the hood</h2>
  <p>React 19 · TypeScript · custom SSE streaming · Zod contracts · an in-house block &amp; canvas library. Full teardown coming to the blog.</p>

  <!--
    Adding media: drop files into public/images/work/strive-gen-ui-chat/ and use one of these.

    <figure>
      <img src="/images/work/strive-gen-ui-chat/slot-canvas.png" alt="Describe what the image shows" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Slot canvas, opened beside a thread</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure>
      <video src="/images/work/strive-gen-ui-chat/streaming.mp4" poster="/images/work/strive-gen-ui-chat/streaming-poster.jpg" controls playsinline preload="none" width="1600" height="900"></video>
      <figcaption>Blocks streaming in, one at a time</figcaption>
    </figure>
  -->

  <aside class="next-up callout wobbly wobbly--2" aria-label="Upcoming write-up">
    <Icon name="pen" />
    <div>
      <strong>Deep dive: streaming generative UI, block by block</strong>
      <p>Parser internals, the tool-call migration, and everything that broke on the way. <span class="soon">Blog landing here soon.</span></p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</WorkLayout>
